      <levelledPara>
        <title>Master BREX for ATA 31-00-00 AMM Data Modules</title>
        <para>
          This Business Rules Exchange (BREX) data module defines the master validation rules
          for all ATA 31 (Indicating/Recording) Aircraft Maintenance Manual (AMM) data modules
          within the AMPEL360AT model documentation.
        </para>
        <para>
          This BREX constrains how ATA 31 AMM DMs are authored, not how they are rendered.
          It enforces structure, semantics, info-code usage, and cross-ATA discipline.
        </para>
        <para>
          This BREX is CSDB-local and inherits from higher-level program BREX.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Applicable Information Codes</title>
        <para>
          The following information codes are permitted in ATA 31 AMM data modules:
        </para>
        <para>
          - 040A: Description
        </para>
        <para>
          - 050A: Crew/Operating Data
        </para>
        <para>
          - 520x: Maintenance Procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          - 72x: Servicing
        </para>
        <para>
          - 73x: Fault Isolation/Testing
        </para>
        <para>
          - 74x: Removal/Installation
        </para>
        <para>
          - 91x: Illustrated Parts Data
        </para>
        <para>
          - 94x: Wiring Data
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Mandatory Sectioning</title>
        <para>
          All ATA 31 AMM procedural data modules must follow this sectioning:
        </para>
        <para>
          1. Description - System/component overview
        </para>
        <para>
          2. Operation - Normal and abnormal operating procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          3. Maintenance - Servicing, inspection, and repair procedures
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Allowed Data Module Types</title>
        <para>
          In the AMM context, the following DM types are permitted:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Descriptive data modules
        </para>
        <para>
          - Procedural data modules
        </para>
        <para>
          - Fault isolation/troubleshooting data modules
        </para>
        <para>
          - Wiring data modules
        </para>
        <para>
          - Illustrated parts data modules (IPD)
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Prohibited Constructs</title>
        <para>
          The following content is prohibited in ATA 31 AMM data modules:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Design claims and rationale (belongs in design documentation)
        </para>
        <para>
          - Certification language and compliance statements (belongs in certification data)
        </para>
        <para>
          - Test procedures for production/qualification (belongs in test procedures)
        </para>
        <para>
          - Marketing or sales content
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Content Inheritance</title>
        <para>
          This BREX layer inherits from:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Program-level BREX (AMPEL360AT general rules)
        </para>
        <para>
          - S1000D Issue 5.0 base BREX
        </para>
        <para>
          Sub-ATA BREX (31-xx-yy) may further constrain these rules.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Scope and Applicability</title>
        <para>
          Scope: ATA 31-00-00 (Indicating/Recording - General)
        </para>
        <para>
          Applies to: Data Modules (DM) only
        </para>
        <para>
          Does not apply to: Publication Modules (PM), rendered outputs (PDF/HTML/IETP)
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
